# heightfieldtomono

- Label: HeightField to Mono
- Category: Copernicus (`Cop`), Houdini 22.0.368
- Inputs: 1 to 1
- Parameters: 6 (exact, read from Houdini by hython)
- Used by the height graph: no

## Feature summary (web, SideFX reference)

- Source: https://www.sidefx.com/docs/houdini/nodes/cop/heightfieldtomono.html
- Summary (EN): Converts a heightfield into a grayscale mono layer: resets the layer type to None and linearly remaps heights from the input range to the output range.
- Résumé (FR) : Convertit un champ de hauteur en couche mono en grisés, en remappant linéairement la plage de hauteurs vers la plage de sortie.

- Inputs meaning: ["height: the original height layer"]

- Key parameters: [{"name": "Compute Range", "meaning": "fills Input Min and Input Max from the layer minimum and maximum heights"}, {"name": "Input Min / Input Max", "meaning": "heights at or below Input Min map to Output Min; at or above Input Max map to Output Max"}, {"name": "Output Min / Output Max", "meaning": "lower and upper ends of the output range"}, {"name": "Clamp to Output Range", "meaning": "limits output values to the output range when enabled"}]

- Caveats: ["By default values outside the input range can extend beyond the output range; enable Clamp to Output Range to prevent this."]

